(Bug #95, the headline repro. `Set zoo to 5.` declares `zoo` a number, so
 the second write is the type-lock violation LANGUAGE.md's "Type
 Immutability" promises to reject. It compiled clean and printed the
 string's ADDRESS as a number: the name's type was never recorded, so the
 lock had nothing to check the write against.)

Set zoo to 5.
Set zoo to "text now".
Print zoo.
